.TH CRS-APP 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-app \- start or stop a DAQ application with its control\-room port assignments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crs\-app
.BR start | stop
.I app\-id
.br
.B crs\-app list
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs on a DAQ host, normally from a desktop launcher inside a VNC
session.
Reads the inventory
.BR apps.yaml (5)
(PyYAML if importable, else a built\-in parser for the flat subset the
file uses), exports
.BI CRS_PORT_ NAME
for every entry of the application's
.B ports
map, and replaces itself with the application's start or stop script via
.BR execve (2):
no arguments, the caller's working directory, inherited standard
streams.
.B DISPLAY
is inherited, so applications open on the session's display.
.PP
The script is looked up first as
.IB $CRS_HOME /bin/ script,
which
.BR install\-controlroom.sh (1)
creates as a
.B symbolic link
into the checkout, and only then as
.IR install_path / script .
Every start script in the suite computes its own directory from
.B ${BASH_SOURCE[0]}
without resolving links, so when the link exists the script looks for
its virtual environment and configuration in
.I ~/controlroom/bin
and fails.
Run the script from its checkout until this is fixed.
.PP
.B list
prints id, repository and ports for every entry, sorted by id.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/controlroom/etc/apps.yaml
inventory.
.TP
.I ~/controlroom/bin/start\-mu2edaq\-*.sh
links made by the installer.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_HOME
install area (default
.IR ~/controlroom ).
.TP
.B CRS_APPS_CONFIG
inventory path (default
.IR $CRS_HOME/etc/apps.yaml ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The application script's exit status after a successful exec; 1 for a
usage error, a missing inventory, an unknown id or a script not found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
crs\-app list
crs\-app start dashboard
CRS_APPS_CONFIG=/tmp/apps.yaml crs\-app stop fts
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-provision\-desktop (1),
.BR install\-controlroom.sh (1),
.BR apps.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq\-app (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
